  "slug": "furcan",
  "name": "FurCan",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurCan is an annual Mexican furry mini con in Puebla City, organized by Furros Puebla. Before it, several furmeets had been held in Puebla, and a group including Tykko Kerensky, Tharos, Bito and Moi set out to organize a larger event, first planned as a furmeet and soon expanded to include workshops, special guests and optional paid registration. The first FurCan was held July 28 to 29, 2018, with over 85 attendees, making it the best-attended furry event in Puebla City. Basic access is free, with optional paid packages adding items such as a t-shirt, button and bracelet, and the event includes movie screenings, drawing contests, video games, a dance contest, an artists' alley and a dealers' den.",
